<p>Apple has <a href="https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/08/apple-announces-special-event-for-october-13-welcome-home/">announced</a> that it&#8217;s planning something for October 13. The assumption—amplified by the &#8220;Welcome Home&#8221; slogan—is that Apple is going to roll out a bunch of new home-oriented products, most notably a touchscreen home hub that&#8217;s been rumored for a couple of years now.</p>
<p>The word broke <a href="https://x.com/gregjoz/status/2108226096407994858">via an X post by Greg Joswiak</a>. Video creator Marques Brownlee <a href="https://x.com/MKBHD/status/2108226481209934307">posted his invitation</a> to an &#8220;Apple Experience&#8221; in Tribeca on October 13 at 9am Eastern.</p>
<p>My understanding is that the &#8220;experience&#8221; at Apple&#8217;s cozy building in Tribeca will focus on creators, while some other traditional press will just receive remote briefings. So I think it&#8217;s wrong to say there will be an Apple Event next Tuesday. More likely, there will be a 9am Eastern drop of a video and a bunch of press releases. Followed shortly by a bunch of influencer videos shot in Apple&#8217;s building, of course.</p>
